student_response:
Thank you for pointing that out—I see now that I shouldn’t be looking at the number of decimal places at all. I just need to divide the distance by the time.

So I’ll do the division:

\[
\text{average speed}= \frac{18.1\ \text{km}}{3.3\ \text{h}}
= \frac{181}{10}\div\frac{33}{10}
= \frac{181}{33}
\approx 5.48\ \text{km/h}.
\]

Rounded to a reasonable number of significant figures, that’s about **5.5 km/h**. 

I’m sorry for the earlier mistake—thanks for the help!

