student_response:
I see what I did wrong now – I was just “multiplying” the numerators and ignoring the denominators.  
When you want a part of a part you have to multiply the whole fractions, keeping both the top and bottom numbers.

So the fraction of the book’s pages that are full‑page color illustrations is  

\[
\frac{5}{8}\times\frac{4}{8}\times\frac{4}{8}
   =\frac{5\cdot4\cdot4}{8\cdot8\cdot8}
   =\frac{80}{512}
   =\frac{5}{32}.
\]

Therefore the correct answer is \(\displaystyle \frac{5}{32}\) of the total pages.

