I went back and checked the conversion factors.

* 1 mile = 5 280 feet  
* 1 hour = 3 600 seconds  

So to change 10 mi / hr to ft / s we multiply by the factor that converts miles to feet and divide by the factor that converts hours to seconds:

\[
10\;\frac{\text{mi}}{\text{hr}}
\;\times\;
\frac{5\,280\;\text{ft}}{1\;\text{mi}}
\;\times\;
\frac{1\;\text{hr}}{3\,600\;\text{s}}
= 10 \times \frac{5\,280}{3\,600}\;\frac{\text{ft}}{\text{s}}
\]

\[
\frac{5\,280}{3\,600}= \frac{44}{30}= \frac{22}{15}\approx 1.4667
\]

Therefore

\[
10 \times 1.4667 \approx 14.667\;\text{ft/s}
\]

Exactly, it’s \(\displaystyle \frac{44}{3}\) ft/s ≈ **14.7 ft/s** (rounded to one decimal place).

